          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01U3H72Pastamr18DQXmFWpe",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022pages/concepts/autoscaling.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Autoscaling\\ndescription: Automatically adjusting the number of running replicas of a service based on observed load.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Autoscaling\\n  - tech/Kubernetes\\n  - pattern/Kubernetes\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Two independent sources; covers Kubernetes-specific mechanisms (HPA, Cluster Autoscaler).\\u0022\\n---\\n\\nAutoscaling adjusts replica count for a service automatically instead of requiring a\\nhuman to resize it manually. The controller observes some signal \\u2014 CPU/memory\\nutilization, queue depth, or a custom metric \\u2014 and computes a desired replica count on\\nan interval.\\n\\n## Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA)\\n\\nThe HPA controller scales the replica count of a Deployment or StatefulSet based on\\nobserved metrics. It polls the metrics API at regular intervals, compares observed\\nvalues (such as CPU or memory utilization) against a target threshold, and computes a\\ndesired replica count.\\n\\nTo prevent rapid scaling up and down (flapping), HPA uses a **stabilization window**.\\nThis window causes the controller to hold at a stable replica count for a period before\\nscaling again, preventing jitter from transient metric spikes or dips.\\n\\nHPA operates at the pod level only \\u2014 it does not provision new nodes when cluster\\ncapacity is exhausted. Node provisioning is handled by the **Cluster Autoscaler**, a\\nseparate controller that scales the underlying infrastructure.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
      "assistant_text": "Good. Now I\u0027ll update the page to add the stabilization window detail and more specific information about HPA. The source provides:\n1. HPA scales based on CPU/memory or custom metrics\n2. It polls metrics API on an interval\n3. Compares against a target\n4. **Computes desired replica count with a stabilization window to avoid flapping** (this is the requested detail)\n5. HPA doesn\u0027t provision nodes (Cluster Autoscaler does)\n\nI\u0027ll integrate these details into the existing page, updating the timestamp and confidence:",
